libmpv: add a Vulkan render API for the gpu-next renderer

Add MPV_RENDER_API_TYPE_VULKAN to the render API. The API user owns the
Vulkan instance and device, mpv imports them into libplacebo, and the
gpu-next renderer draws into a VkImage that the API user passes for each
frame. With Vulkan, gpu-next can run compute shaders (//!COMPUTE), which
the OpenGL 4.1 context on macOS cannot.

Source: the header render_vk.h and the device import in libmpv_vk.c come
from mpv_kit (https://github.com/TATboy210/mpv_kit, MIT license, commit
c6ea8a34ea42), patches 0001 to 0004. They are adapted for IINA:
  * The render backend is the gpu-next backend from mpv pull request
    #18607 (patch 18607-libmpv-gpu-next-opengl.patch), not mpv_kit's
    changes to vo_gpu_next.c. This patch applies after 18607.
  * The legacy gpu renderer does not accept the Vulkan API type.
  * The target color space works as in the OpenGL backend: the image is
    an sRGB surface, and target-trc, target-prim and target-peak override
    it. So HDR10 output works with target-trc=pq into a 10-bit image.
    mpv dithers to the bit depth of the image format.
  * Not included: --hwdec=vulkan support for imported devices (mpv_kit
    0002), because macOS uses VideoToolbox, and the shader cache (0003),
    because the gpu-next renderer of 18607 already sets one.
---
